\begin_layout Standard
We believe neither of these situations serves the goal of giving users the freedom to understand and use their systems to their maximum potential.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Software documentation should be accessible,
 engaging,
 helpful,
 and to the extent possible given the nature of software development,
 complete.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Much modern documentation emerges from pipelines divorced from both the software's creators and its users.
 While we accept the validity of these approaches in the industry we also insist that it is not the only way to arrive at our shared goals:
 there remains space for expansive and useful documentation,
 crafted by human beings with intentionality and care.
 Bismarck supposedly said 
\begin_inset Quotes bld
\end_inset

laws are like sausages:
 it's better not to see them being made
\begin_inset Quotes brd
\end_inset

.
 We think that this is unlike our situation:
 The Manual's source is available,
 the tool chain is clearly described.
 Documentation is not like sausages:
 it is better when we can all see it being made and take part in the process.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Manual is the result of our efforts to pursue these ideals for Snapshot Manager.
\end_layout

