\begin_layout Section
Milestone III:
 Snapshot Inspection and Comparison (2025)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The ability to interact with snapshot sets on the running system,
 as well as to find and visualise the differences between two snapshot sets,
 or between a snapshot set and the running system had been a core feature of the proposal since the earliest conceptions of the Snapshot Manager project.
 To create these kinds of tools,
 however,
 you need a firm base on which to build.
 The previous milestone deliveries put the project in a good place to finally begin hacking away at these features in the summer of 2025.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Milestone IIIa:
 The Mount Manager
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Key to enabling the advanced features we were interested in was the ability to automatically mount snapshot sets as a coherent file system view on the running host,
 and to be able to fire off commands to run 
\begin_inset Flex Emph
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
inside
\end_layout

\end_inset

 the mounted snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The mount manager is the subsystem that enables this.
 It is responsible for discovering,
 mounting,
 and unmounting file systems from snapshot sets in the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
/run/snapm/mounts
\end_layout

\end_inset

 directory.
 It abstracts all the messy details of parsing the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
