\begin_layout Section
Care and Feeding of Your Snapshot Set
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Now that you have a snapshot set that captures the state of your system at some moment in time you need to know how to look after it.
 This is essentially the same task as you would need to carry out for any other volume managed with your tool of choice.
 The major point to bear in mind is that both thin and LVM2 CoW snapshots can run out of space.
 It is important to ensure that this does not happen for the reasons explained in chapter 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
