\end_layout

\begin_layout Quotation
\begin_inset Quotes bld
\end_inset

All human wisdom is summed up in these two words:
 Wait,
 and Hope.
\begin_inset Quotes brd
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\size scriptsize
—
 Edmond Dantès,
 
\begin_inset Quotes bld
\end_inset

The Count of Monte Cristo
\begin_inset Quotes brd
\end_inset

,
 by Alexandre Dumas,
 1844.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Snapshot Manager includes a dedicated subsystem for reporting progress on long running operations (for example,
 file system 
\begin_inset Flex Emph
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
diff
\end_layout

\end_inset

 operations that can take minutes for large subtrees).
 The progress system is integrated with the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm
\end_layout

\end_inset

 logger so that log messages that are interleaved with progress reports are not lost and are always displayed on the terminal.
 Long running processes can be interrupted with the standard 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Ctrl-C
\end_layout

\end_inset

 sequence (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
SIGINT
\end_layout

\end_inset

 / Python 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
KeyboardInterrupt
\end_layout

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
By default progress indicators are displayed using Unicode characters and terminal control operations (
\begin_inset Flex Emph
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
escape sequences
\end_layout

\end_inset

) where available.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Programmatic progress reporting support (for example,
 writing progress notifications to a nominated file descriptor,
 or emitting DBus or other IPC signals) may be added in a future release.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The operations that are tracked via progress indicators take a variable amount of time depending on the options given,
 the amount of work to do,
 and the capabilities of the system on which they run:
 in some cases,
 for large operations,
 this may take several minutes.
 If you find yourself waiting for such an operation,
 so long as the throbber is throbbing or the progress bar is progressing simply 
\nospellcheck on

