\begin_layout Standard
The 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Manager
\end_layout

\end_inset

 class is the core orchestrator in Snapshot Manager.
 It is responsible for loading plugins,
 discovering snapshot sets,
 initialising the mount manager,
 scheduler,
 boot cache and other core subsystems.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Manager
\end_layout

\end_inset

 aggregates instances of Scheduler,
 Mounts,
 and BootCache,
 and maintains the global lists of plugins,
 disabled plugins,
 and snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Users of the API should instantiate the Manager class before performing any snapshot management operations (for example,
 calling the procedural API defined in 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm.command
\end_layout

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Manager
\end_layout

\end_inset

 updates its own internal state when its methods are used to perform operations on snapshot sets (for example,
 creating,
 deleting,
 renaming etc.).
 If operations are performed outside the manager,
 client code should call the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Manager.discover_snapshot_sets()
\end_layout

\end_inset

 method to refresh the internal state.
\end_layout

