\begin_layout Section
Overview
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The difference engine is our most complex and expensive algorithm,
 and also therefore the most interesting.
 Much of what 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm
\end_layout

\end_inset

 does amounts to mere abstraction and automation.
 The difference engine has a little more to it.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This chapter explains the algorithms and internals of the Difference Engine:
 
\begin_inset Formula $O(n)$
\end_inset

 diff generation and move detection
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The diff generation and move detection process itself is 
\begin_inset Formula $O(n)$
\end_inset

 however the overall 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
compare_roots()
\end_layout

\end_inset

 operation is 
\begin_inset Formula $O(n\log n)$
\end_inset

 due to the need to sort paths before computing differences.
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 as well as difference tree construction and rendering.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Difference Engine is implemented in the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm.fsdiff
\end_layout

\end_inset

 package and consists of ten Python modules:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
cache
\end_layout

\end_inset

 —
 The 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
diffcache
\end_layout

\end_inset

:
 improves performance of consecutive runs with the same targets and options.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
changes
\end_layout

\end_inset

 —
 File changes and change detection
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
