\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Under Pressure:
 RSS Safety Limits
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
By default the difference engine will check its own memory consumption at two points in the difference computation and caching process,
 and will refuse to proceed with difference computation or writing the compressed cache image if content diffs are enabled and the builtin memory usage thresholds are exceeded:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Immediately after constructing 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
tree_a
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
tree_b
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and before calling
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
DiffEngine.compute_diff()
\end_layout

\end_inset

 to compute difference records (the most expensive part of the algorithm in memory terms when content diffs are enabled).
 This check is implemented in the
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm.fsdiff.fsdiffer._should_diff()
\end_layout

\end_inset

 function.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Immediately before writing the compressed cache image after difference records have been computed.
 This check is implemented in the
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm.fsdiff.cache._should_cache()
\end_layout

\end_inset

 function.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The limit for the first of these is triggered when 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm
\end_layout

\end_inset

's RSS (resident set size) as measured by the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
VmRSS
\end_layout

\end_inset

 field of 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
/proc/self/status
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
proc_pid_status(5)
\end_layout

\end_inset

) exceeds one third (33.3%) of available physical memory after tree construction.
 The second is triggered when 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm
\end_layout

\end_inset

's RSS exceeds 60.0% of available physical memory prior to writing the cache.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These limits were determined through empirical torture testing
\begin_inset Foot
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Whole root file system diffs in situations where large volumes of changes are present,
 for example following significant software updates.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 on low memory systems (2-4GiB) with slow or absent swap devices.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The reasoning for the first limit is that when content diffs are enabled an unknown (and potentially large) number of content diffs of unknown sizes must be stored in memory.
 If our memory usage already exceeds one third of the available memory before performing that computation it is possible that the additional memory requirements will push the system into swap congestion or trigger the Out of Memory (OOM) killer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The rationale for the cache limit is that when writing compressed data to the cache the Python 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
pickle
\end_layout

\end_inset

 library must first write a binary representation of the current object into memory before handing it to the compressor library.
 If memory usage is approaching two thirds of that available then there is again the possibility that this additional memory consumption may push the system towards undesirable behaviour.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
--no-mem-check
\end_layout

\end_inset

 option (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
DiffOptions.no_mem_check
\end_layout

\end_inset

) exists to allow the administrator to bypass these checks.
 Use with caution!
 In most cases it is better to diff smaller subtrees of the file system in successive diff operations than it is to disable the memory pressure checks and hope for the best.
\end_layout

