\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Flex Strong
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Q:
\end_layout

\end_inset

 What happens if I reboot while a revert is in progress?
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Flex Strong
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
A:
\end_layout

\end_inset

 The revert will continue the next time that its volumes are activated.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Flex Strong
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Q:
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Do I need to create boot entries manually?
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Flex Strong
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
A:
\end_layout

\end_inset

 No:
 use the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
-b/--bootable
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
-r/--revert
\end_layout

\end_inset

 options when creating snapshot sets and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
snapm
\end_layout

\end_inset

 will take care of the necessary details.
\end_layout

