\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Flex Strong
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Q:
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Is it safe to snapshot a running database?
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Flex Strong
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
A:
\end_layout

\end_inset

 It depends on your definition of 
\begin_inset Quotes bld
\end_inset

safe
\begin_inset Quotes brd
\end_inset

:
 the resulting snapshot will be internally consistent at the file system level but the database data will almost certainly not be 
\begin_inset Flex Emph
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
application
\end_layout

\end_inset

 consistent.
 Refer to section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:The-Concept-of"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

 and chapter 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "chap:Crash-Consistency-vs."
