 My diff command is taking forever —
 is this normal?
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Flex Strong
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
A:
\end_layout

\end_inset

 The time taken for difference computation is proportional to the size of the file system (number of files and directories) and the degree of change between the volumes being compared.
 It is normal for difference calculations for large volumes with many changes to take some time (minutes to tens of minutes for very large file systems).
 You may be able to gain more insight into what is happening by enabling verbose logs and debugging.
