Implementing Comprehensive Snapshot Management for Linux - 20th July 2023
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Problem Statement
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Managing storage snapshots in Linux is fragmented and lacks a unified solution,
 leading to complexities in capturing,
 managing,
 and utilising snapshots across different implementations.
 Users face challenges in creating multi volume snapshot sets,
 performing life cycle management,
 inspecting snapshot data,
 and coordinating applications during snapshot operations.
 This fragmentation hinders system administration,
 backup strategies,
 troubleshooting,
 and efficient utilisation of snapshots.
 There is a need for a comprehensive snapshot management system for Linux that provides a higher level interface,
 simplifies snapshot operations,
 supports various mechanisms,
 and enhances overall usability and administration of storage snapshots.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Goal
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The goal of this project is to develop a robust and user friendly snapshot management system for Linux that addresses the existing challenges and provides a unified and efficient solution for
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
capturing,
 managing,
 and utilising storage snapshots.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Milestone I (MVP)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
User Story:
 Capture Snapshots
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a system administrator,
 I want to capture snapshots on demand for a user specified list of volumes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Implement an intuitive command line interface (CLI) for snapshot creation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Provide support for capturing snapshots across different snapshot mechanisms,
 such as LVM,
 Stratis,
 and Btrfs.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Ensure the ability to capture multiple volumes simultaneously and create consistent snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
User Story:
 Efficient Management
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a system administrator,
 I want to manage snapshot sets efficiently.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enable deletion of previously captured snapshot sets to free up storage space.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Implement a list command to display available snapshot sets and their associated volumes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Integrate snapshot merging functionality where supported by the snapshot mechanisms.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
User Story:
 Bootable Snapshots
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a system administrator,
 I want to create bootable snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Utilise boom to manage auxiliary boot entries for seamless booting from snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Implement mechanisms to ensure the integrity and consistency of bootable snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
MVP Timeline
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Approximately six months of development by a dedicated developer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Milestone II (Scheduling)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
User Story:
 Scheduled Creation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a system administrator,
 I want to schedule automatic creation of snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Add the ability to schedule regular or recurring snapshot creation for specified volumes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Provide options for customisable scheduling parameters,
 such as frequency and retention policies.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
User Story:
 Garbage Collection
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a system administrator,
 I want to perform life cycle management of snapshot sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Implement automatic garbage collection of snapshot sets based on defined policies and criteria.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Allow users to set retention periods,
 maximum snapshot counts,
 or space based policies.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Milestone II Timeline
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Approximately six months of development by a dedicated developer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Milestone III (Inspection & Comparison)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Snapshot Inspection and Comparison
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
User Story:
 Inspection
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a system administrator,
 I want to inspect and interact with snapshot data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Develop mechanisms to mount and chroot into a previous system state from snapshots.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enable running commands within the mounted snapshot to troubleshoot or extract data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
User Story:
 Comparison
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a system administrator,
 I want to compare snapshots and view changes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Implement a comparison tool to visualise the differences between two snapshots.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Enable efficient tracking of changes to help identify and understand system modifications.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Milestone III Timeline
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Approximately six to twelve months of development by a dedicated developer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Milestone IV (Application Coordination)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Application coordination for the creation of 
